    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2Eefh2qhtKyNPtKFWfLMcko)_\n\n## What\n\n- `sp-litnotes-titles` falls back to `pub-editor` when a note has no `pub-author` (collections, proceedings, but not only).\n  - `pub-author` always wins; an ambiguous `pub-author` does not fall back.\n  - Several editors are read and shortened like authors (`A and B`, `A, B and C`, `A, B et al.`).\n  - Title looks the same as for authors: `Lee and Roe (2014) Essays`. There was no existing marker convention, so no `(ed.)` by default.\n  - New option `sp-litnotes-titles-editor-suffix` (e.g. `\" (ed.)\"`) adds a marker for editor-based titles only.\n  - With BibTeX on (`missing`/`always`), the entry's `editor` field is used when neither the note nor the entry has authors.\n- Reports: the \"no author\" reason now mentions `pub-editor`; failed rows show the `pub-editor` value; BibTeX-derived editors are listed as \"editors\".\n- Docs (bullets) updated in `docs/tangles/funct/sp-org-lint.org`, `.el` kept in sync. No CHANGELOG edit.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Emacs 29 batch: 20/20 ERT tests in `sp-litnotes-titles-test.el` pass, including a new test for editor fallback, author priority, ambiguous author and the suffix.\n- The bibtex tests needed stubs for `sp-var-dir`, `sp-cache-dir` and `sp-author-notes-latex-to-unicode` in my bare batch run.\n- Not run on the real vault; the BibTeX `editor` path has no dedicated test.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi8kqneBVR5xsKkgAYw)_",
